{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs each system once:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Ordering Systems","level":3,"anchor":"Ordering-Systems","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or before one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written earlier, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its written place:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to throw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","level":3,"anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two systems ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L100"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Schedule","roleHeading":"Structure"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Creating a Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilde